        <mxCell id="c75" value="The invoice settled" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="407.48" y="624" width="110.044" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c76" value="&lt;i&gt;Test S6 for the largest refund, RF-2025-000097 (17,745.96) of the largest credit, CM-2025-000255: each document in the lane of the department whose people recorded, received or approved it, at its date, as the Timeline sheet lists them (the invoice is billing&#x27;s, as the sheet puts it; no table records who prepared it). The credit was posted all to 2060, so 13,081.41 of the invoice was still unpaid on the credit date and on the refund date, 1 day after the invoice was due and before the applications of its last two receipts. The records show what happened and in what order, not why: the refund is a follow-up, not a conclusion.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="652" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
